## Multi-chain RPC

### POST /v1/rpc/{network}
Multi-chain JSON-RPC — **one endpoint, 40 chains**. Swap `{network}` for any chain: `ethereum`, `base`, `solana`, `polygon`, `bsc`, `arbitrum`, `optimism`, `avalanche`, `zksync`, `bitcoin`, `xrp`, `polkadot`, `near`, `sui`, and more (aliases like `eth`, `arb`, `avax` work too). Standard `jsonrpc: "2.0"` body, EVM (`eth_*`) and non-EVM (`getSlot`, …) methods. **$0.003 per call** (a JSON-RPC batch is priced per element); hot reads are cached. No API key — pay-per-call in USDC.
Example: `curl -X POST https://blockrun.ai/v1/rpc/ethereum -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"eth_blockNumber","id":1}'`

### POST /v1/solana/rpc
Pay-per-call Solana JSON-RPC. Routed to a hardened cluster with response caching for common reads. Standard `jsonrpc: "2.0"` body. Per-method price returned in 402 body before commit. (Also available via the unified `/v1/rpc/solana`.)

