## ClawRouter — Smart LLM Router (Open Source)

MIT-licensed router that sits between your agent and any LLM provider. 84% cheaper than pinning one flagship for every request (98% on `eco`), via 7-layer prompt compression, intelligent model routing, and response caching.

```bash
npm install -g @blockrun/clawrouter
openclaw plugins install @blockrun/clawrouter   # or, as an OpenClaw plugin
```

GitHub: https://github.com/BlockRunAI/ClawRouter

### ClawRouter plugins — put the router inside your harness

Adapters that give an existing agent harness the whole catalog from one wallet. None of them reimplement routing; they wire a harness to ClawRouter.

**dsh-clawrouter** — plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DeepSeek AI's open-source harness; the plugin is BlockRun's). Headline feature is a safety review gate: a stronger model reads flagged tool calls before the executor runs them and answers safe / dangerous / uncertain, failing to a human and never open. Measured on 0.9.0, 2026-08-14: fired on 0 of 59 ordinary commands, missed 0 of 39 destructive ones, $0.0048 and ~3s when it fires.
```bash
dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-clawrouter
```
https://blockrun.ai/clawrouter/dsh · npm: dsh-clawrouter

**ClawRouter for Hermes** — plugin for NousResearch Hermes. Replaces one provider block per lab with a single local endpoint; also sidesteps two upstream auxiliary-vision bugs as a side effect. Python, on PyPI.
```bash
pip install hermes-plugin-clawrouter
```
https://blockrun.ai/clawrouter/hermes · PyPI: hermes-plugin-clawrouter

**clawrouter-codex** — bridge for OpenAI Codex, which speaks only the Responses API. Translates `/v1/responses` onto chat completions. Direct mode (default) holds the wallet key and pays x402 itself; proxy mode delegates that to a local ClawRouter. Streaming is synthesized rather than incremental, reasoning items are dropped, and it is stateless.
```bash
npx @blockrun/clawrouter-codex up
```
https://blockrun.ai/clawrouter/codex · npm: @blockrun/clawrouter-codex

